<spell-notebook "shape theming">
	<header level="1">
		Shape
		<header>A shape is a three dimensional object displayed on a two dimensional plane.</>
	</>
	<shape-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-shape-*` tokens on the shape or any ancestor; `::part(shape)` works too. Style the
			pieces with `::part()`: `shape` (the stage, with the 3D perspective) and `sides` (the box that turns) on the
			shape, `side` (the face) on each `<ui-side>`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-shape[cube] {
			  --ui-shape-cube-size: 10em;
			}
			ui-side::part(side) {
			  border-radius: 0.5em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`duration` on a shape beats `--ui-shape-duration`. Never set the `--_ui-*` names (`--_ui-shape-type` is how
				the sides learn their shape's type): they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-shape" playground>
				<button type="button" class="ui button" commandfor="shape-demo-plain-playground" command="--next">Flip left</>
				<ui-shape id="shape-demo-plain-playground">
					<ui-side>
						<p>This side starts visible.</>
					</>
					<ui-side>
						<p>This is yet another side.</>
					</>
					<ui-side>
						<p>This is the last side.</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) restyles the cards, headers and images
			on a shape's sides.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
